  "id": "07",
  "name": "Mining of metal ores",
  "section": "B",
  "summary": "Metal miners report AI in exploration targeting, autonomous haulage and drilling, remote operations centres, ore sorting, process-plant optimisation, predictive maintenance and safety monitoring, usually with the stated aim of removing people from hazardous areas. On the demand side, copper, silver, tin and rare-earth producers cite AI data centres, grid build-out, semiconductors and robotics, and uranium miners point to hyperscaler nuclear deals and data-centre power needs. Workforce change, union and community reactions to automation and cyber exposure of autonomous systems are the risk themes.",
